    "body": "I don't think spec \"switches\" are defined rigorously enough to say whether they must be exhaustive or not. It's reasonable to interpret the current text as just not performing any steps when the value doesn't hit any of the cases.\r\n\r\nHowever, if there is a reasonable thing to assert in the null case (which occurs for [navigable creation/destruction updates](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#update-for-navigable-creation/destruction)), then we could add a clause there.",
